"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project has received a $2M budget approval and is expanding its team with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, joining in an onboarding session on September 10th. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase using AI algorithms, to be discussed on August 5th. The project recently completed its testing phase and design phase, moving into development under lead developer Omar Jensen. A prototype for secure file sharing has been tested ahead of schedule, with UI enhancements planned for October. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated starting next January. A celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
